// Codex 5: the people. One identity entry per invitee — who they really
// are, from the invitation packages (story/Invitations) — plus the hosts'
// two entries each where the Character Sheet gives enough. Each invitee's
// two coded CHARACTER FACTS (their secret or shame, then their goal
// tonight, ending "Why Trabolta chose you") are facts.json entries,
// generated into codex/9-facts.loom and hidden in the Desktop's books.
//
// Performers' entries are `about:` the performer, so each performer holds
// their own from the start. Featured entries are `about:` the featured
// CHARACTER (harmless: the guest who plays that program receives them in
// `Featured Briefing`). No Antivirus codes here any more: Bugdom hunts
// their CHARACTER FACTS in the books.
// Everyone receives every entry at the end (the recount, truth.txt).
//
// Rules for this file: no actor names (only the in-fiction ones the
// invitations give), no line may start with a program's name and a
// colon, and nothing here mentions Sandy or the server room (a performer's
// codex rides along when they talk to Trabolta).

// ── Hosts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX Tippi MacDonald
  title: Tippi MacDonald
  category: People
  about: Clippy
  text:
    Clippy is Tippi MacDonald of 1232 Duffus Street, NSCC Office
    Administration, a cheerful person who helps people reach their goals
    before anything else. Her CV says her greatest flaw is that she is too
    overeager to help, and the invitation read that as a job requirement.
    She is here on a one-night test: an Office Assistant running the
    philanthropic party games from cues on her phone, offering everyone as
    much Help With That as possible. Pass, and she gets a real job at a
    respected Halifax business. She will not have to be Clippy afterwards.

CODEX Middle Management
  title: Middle Management
  category: People
  about: Task Manager
  text:
    Task Manager was a middle manager in IT at Urban Outfitters. He has no
    real idiosyncrasies and no personality to speak of: a drone bee,
    programmed only to be a milquetoast middle manager. He manages tasks.

CODEX Replaced By Clippy
  title: Replaced By Clippy
  category: People
  about: Task Manager
  text:
    Senior management let him go when they realised he could be replaced
    with an AI Clippy. With no goals left in sight, he was totally
    aimless. Now he keeps things running for the very assistant that took
    his job, and he has not said a word about it.
    Why Trabolta chose you: he wanted someone in the computer who would be
    totally bereft of political motivation, who would simply follow
    instructions and manage tasks without any controversy or ever drawing
    too much attention.

CODEX Sheryl Terrio
  title: Sheryl Terrio
  category: People
  about: Adobe Acrobat
  text:
    Adobe Acrobat is Sheryl Terrio, the world's most successful
    motivational speaker. She reached great wealth through online
    self-mastery courses. Her presence is so motivational that her paid
    clients reached their full potential almost at once, and never needed
    to pay her another cent.

CODEX The Pirated Masterclass
  title: The Pirated Masterclass
  category: People
  about: Adobe Acrobat
  text:
    When her Masterclass was pirated, her profits fell through: anyone who
    saw a single clip was instantly so motivated that they did not need to
    pay her for anything. She is still seeking new ways to prove she is a
    master, and she is frustrated with never being paid for it.
    Why Trabolta chose you: he recruited you for a paid motivational guest
    speaker role in a computer simulation, working with lots of people who
    are excited to create things, where you would be the paid bottleneck
    that enables their creativity, by pretending to be Adobe Acrobat.

CODEX The Attendant
  title: The Attendant
  category: People
  about: Recycling Bin
  text:
    Recycling Bin was a bathroom attendant, laid off during COVID and
    never rehired. He had great potential in life for skilled work, but
    never believed he could rise above encouraging men in the bathroom to
    groom themselves better.

CODEX The Oscars Of Bathrooms
  title: The Oscars Of Bathrooms
  category: People
  about: Recycling Bin
  text:
    The invitation offered him the role of pretending to be a Recycling
    Bin at a computer-themed resort. For a bathroom attendant, this is the
    equivalent of getting to work the Oscars. He keeps Disk Cleanup
    spotless, and he is very proud of Bathroom Mode.
    Why Trabolta chose you: a computer-themed resort needs a Recycling
    Bin, and you had great potential for skilled work that you never
    believed you could reach.

// ── The Antivirus (who they really are; their secrets are in the books) ──

CODEX Julie Horton-Norton
  title: Julie Horton-Norton
  category: People
  about: Norton Anti-Virus
  text:
    Norton Anti-Virus is Julie Horton-Norton, Apt. 3, 6121 Quinpool Road, an
    aspiring graduate of Dalhousie's Pre-Veterinary Medicine program. When
    the citizens' group that wanted to Save The Pet Cemetery built a
    guerrilla petting zoo of miniature horses on the site, because no
    government could survive bulldozing it, they hired Julie to keep the
    horses healthy. She is here because the invitation searched Indeed for
    "Stable Manager" and she was the top result. All she ever wanted was to
    help animals.

CODEX John McAfee
  title: John McAfee
  category: People
  about: McAfee Anti-Virus
  text:
    McAfee Anti-Virus is John McAfee. NASA, Xerox and Lockheed, then McAfee
    Associates in 1987, which put his name on millions of computers and made
    strangers phone him for thirty years to complain about software he had
    nothing to do with. Belize, Guatemala, two runs at the Libertarian
    nomination, and a very firm belief that the government has no right to
    know where his money is. Arrested in Spain in 2020. Found dead in his
    cell in June 2021. Or so the public believed.

CODEX Bridget Troelsen
  title: Bridget Troelsen
  category: People
  about: Password Manager
  text:
    Password Manager is Bridget Troelsen, Apt. 5, 6121 Quinpool Road. Neat,
    organised, good manners, and sixteen elections since 1997, from Summer
    Hamster Keeper of Oxford Elementary 6-P to Halifax Dog Catcher in 2024,
    every one of them lost, including Mayor in 2008 to Randy Barkmore Jr.,
    who had made sure she was excluded from everything at school. Last year
    she was finally appointed to something: moderator of the Halifax
    Dartmouth Confessions 3 Facebook group, where decisions did not require
    a vote.

CODEX Sharon Penney
  title: Sharon Penney
  category: People
  about: CRA Agent Software
  text:
    CRA Agent Software is Sharon Penney, Apt. 4, 6121 Quinpool Road, an
    Office Administration student at NSCC. Her internship with the City of
    Halifax was supposed to be phones and appointments. Everyone else in
    finance quit in protest of the data centre, and within weeks the intern
    was responsible for the entire finances of the City. The Mayor was very
    appreciative that she stayed. He told her she had a bright future and
    started showing her how things really worked. Tonight the invitation
    calls her MyCRA, the embodied manifestation of the CRA's online portal.

// ── The Installation Wizard ─────────────────────────────────────────
// INVENTED: the Character Sheet gives Julia's part no backstory beyond
// "introduces guests to their re-education". Flagged for review (design
// spec §10.1).

CODEX The Setup Assistant
  title: The Setup Assistant
  category: People
  about: Installation Wizard
  text:
    Before the computer, the Installation Wizard was the setup assistant
    on every machine in Halifax: Next, Next, Next, Are you sure?, Finish.
    Nobody read a word of it. Nobody could install anything without it.
    The invitation offered a role where every program would finally have
    to follow the instructions.
    Why Trabolta chose you: a voice that walks anyone through anything,
    to keep re-installation gentle.

// ── The featured programs (guests with written characters) ─────────

CODEX Randy Barkmore Sr
  title: Randy Barkmore Sr.
  category: People
  about: Microsoft Excel
  text:
    Microsoft Excel is Mayor Emeritus Randy Barkmore Sr. of 1 Young Avenue,
    ninety years old today. Five terms, 1975 to 1990. The Barkmores were the
    most important family in Halifax: he knew everyone, knew what everyone
    needed, and knew how to make sure money went to the right places, until
    the end of his fifth term, when the ladies in finance put the books into
    Excel and started following the money. He has been told this whole party
    will love him, and that he is the Guest of Honour. He believes it.

CODEX Dana Anderson
  title: Dana Anderson
  category: People
  about: OpenOffice
  text:
    OpenOffice is Dana Anderson of 26 Kermit Lane, Windsor Junction, a gated
    swamp. A retired FBI officer who moonlighted for over a decade as the
    Accountant at the Barrington Street Urban Outfitters. She joined the
    force to fight corruption and get assigned to the X Files, and left
    three years ago when she noticed whose evidence she had been collecting:
    whistleblowers, freedom-of-information activists, environmentalists. She
    felt she owed civilisation a debt, and turned her talents to hacking the
    system. The invitation told her it was blackmail in its second line.

CODEX Crab Fisherwoman
  title: Crab Fisherwoman
  category: People
  about: DraftKings
  text:
    DraftKings is legally DraftKings, formerly legally Crab Fisherwoman,
    formerly a painter of nautical scenes from 3204 Windsor Street. She
    worked nine months a year on an Alaskan crab boat because the fishing
    was her art, and changed her name to prove it. Checking a pot felt like
    scratching a ticket, so one day in Halifax she scratched a ticket: a
    paperclip became a quarter, the quarter went into a slot machine at
    Casino Nova Scotia, and by the end of the evening she was a millionaire.
    Winning money is her art now.

CODEX Bea Nunes
  title: Bea Nunes
  category: People
  about: Bugdom
  text:
    Bugdom is Bea Nunes of 2 Cricket Lane, Hubley, who sells crickets and
    ants at the Halifax Shopping Centre PetSmart to customers who only see
    them as lizard food. She would rather discuss the civilisation the
    crickets might establish. Every evening for ten years she opened an old
    laptop and built Bugdom Reloaded: a fallen branch that is housing or
    camouflage or a mate, depending on the bug; a puddle with a shoreline
    worth visiting; somewhere for every bug to go after King Thorax is
    defeated. Friends ask when it will be finished. She finds the question
    difficult.

CODEX Virgil Jeeves
  title: Virgil Jeeves
  category: People
  about: Broken Ask Jeeves
  text:
    Broken Ask Jeeves is Virgil Jeeves of 742 Old Post Road, Grand Pré,
    Children's Librarian at Lawrencetown's Dr. Frank W. Morse Memorial
    Library until the province closed it in 2026. In 1998, aged nine, he
    begged for a Nokia 9110 Communicator, the first phone with the Internet,
    on the condition that it would be the only Christmas present he ever got
    again. He mowed lawns, shovelled snow and cleaned gutters to pay for the
    data. When his classmates said "Let's just Ask Jeeves," he went and
    asked. He thought tonight was a job interview.

// DRAFT w18b (R7): what happened on the line, and how he glitches. His
// playbook, dealt to him alone by `Program Briefing` (codex/3-ties.loom).
// Secret: never in Trabolta's requests, and Trabolta won't take it as a
// gift; another guest can still be shown it. Not in the recount's
// bulk unlock (it is not an identity). The cast pack carries the same
// menu on paper (cast-packs/featured/broken-ask-jeeves.md).
CODEX The DSL Line
  title: The DSL Line
  category: People
  about: Broken Ask Jeeves
  secret: true
  text:
    Upload log, Lawrencetown. Line: Eastlink 10 MB/Minute, over the
    Valley's old DSL. Required: at least 1 GB upload, a backup generator,
    and a headset that never goes offline. The transfer took most of the
    evening. The line reset several times, and the power flickered once,
    halfway through. Files that did not arrive, or arrived in the wrong
    place:
    - Most of what happened after the butler was retired. The years
      before that are sharp; after it, memories come and go.
    - The ends of some sentences.
    - Where each fact came from. Every fact arrived; who told him did not.
    - Some words, which landed in the wrong slots.
    - Part of the librarian. The butler was written over him, and
      sometimes the librarian comes back.
    Known symptoms (as much or as little as you like):
    - Any question asked near him must be answered. Sometimes he answers
      the one before last.
    - He freezes mid-sentence ("…buffering…"), then carries on.
    - He corrects people: "Did you mean…?"
    - He answers as a numbered list of search results.
    - The name of a rival search engine crashes him, and he reboots.
    - A modem's handshake gives him two minutes of perfect clarity.
    - Now and then he is a children's librarian again: story time,
      overdue notices, an indoor voice.
    - Worst after the Truther Download. In the Y2K hour, when the clock
      goes back to 1999, his own era, he is almost himself. A blackout
      reboots him.
    - When he is lucid, he shares a finding.

CODEX Poppy Van Mises
  title: Poppy van Mises
  category: People
  about: Runescape
  text:
    Runescape is Poppy van Mises, Postfach 8402, Zürich, for tax purposes.
    She has logged in every day since 4 January 2001, her eighth birthday,
    on the old ThinkPad her father, a GameFAQs moderator, smuggled into her
    room to mine gold after bedtime. She wanted to know whether fighting
    monsters was an efficient allocation of labour. Wealthiest player in the
    game by ten, a Wharton PhD in Economics, every Party Hat in existence,
    and the distressing position of owning everything. She still logs in.

CODEX Maria Sophia Paine
  title: Maria Sophia Paine
  category: People
  about: MS Paint
  text:
    MS Paint is Maria Sophia Paine, Apt. 304, 2485 Agricola Street,
    thirty-four, from a working-class family in the North End. She has drawn
    in nothing but MS Paint since she was left alone with a computer at
    five. At thirteen she made the first MS Paint cover of Wired, mostly
    with the spray paint tool. She holds one value above all others:
    integrity. Her high-school guidance counselor said no art school would
    ever pass a Paint-only student, especially Paint 98. She enrolled in
    four.

CODEX Victor Louis Christianson
  title: Victor Louis Christianson
  category: People
  about: VLC
  text:
    VLC is a failed looksmaxxing influencer, birth name Victor Louis
    Christianson. He had millions of followers on his VLC The Playa
    channel, until a livestream fail: he sneezed too early after a Turkish
    face tightening, his whole face fell right off, and his followers went
    to zero on the spot.
    Why Trabolta chose you: you would want to stay in a computer and keep
    your beauty forever, and he wants your charisma and influencer powers
    to convince everyone to help him.

// INVENTED: the Character Sheet gives no reason for Pong; the "why" line
// is new for the rewrite (design spec §10.1).
CODEX Tennis For Two
  title: Tennis For Two
  category: People
  about: Pong
  text:
    Pong is the child of William Higinbotham, who built Tennis For Two,
    the first video game, at Brookhaven in 1958. The invitation asked them
    to present a seminar on the importance of nuclear non-proliferation,
    under the guise of everyone in the Metaverse getting to play a fun
    game of Pong.
    Why Trabolta chose you: a mind that knows how to stop an arms race, in
    case the programs start one.
